wledge and scope of the model. See <a href=3D"https://cloud.google.com/vert=
ex-ai/generative-ai/docs/model-reference/function-calling">Function calling=
</a>.</p></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><p><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">toolConfig</code></p></td>
    <td><p>Optional. See <a href=3D"https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/gene=
rative-ai/docs/model-reference/function-calling">Function calling</a>.</p><=
/td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><p><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">safetySettings</code></p></td=
>
    <td><p>Optional: <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">SafetySetting</code=
></p><p>Per request settings for blocking unsafe content.</p><p>Enforced on=
 <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">GenerateContentResponse.candidates</cod=
e>.</p></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><p><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">generationConfig</code></p></=
td>
    <td><p>Optional: <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">GenerationConfig</c=
ode></p><p>Generation configuration settings.</p></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><p><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">labels</code></p></td>
    <td><p>Optional: <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">string</code></p><p=
>Metadata that you can add to the API call in the format of key-value pairs=
.</p></td>
  </tr>
</tbody></table></div>

<h4 id=3D"contents" data-text=3D"contents" tabindex=3D"-1" role=3D"presenta=
tion"><span class=3D"devsite-heading" role=3D"heading" aria-level=3D"4"><co=
de translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">contents</code></span><button type=3D"butto=
n" class=3D"devsite-heading-link button-flat material-icons" aria-label=3D"=
Copy link to this section: contents" data-title=3D"Copy link to this sectio=
n: contents" data-id=3D"contents"></button></h4>

<p>The base structured data type containing multi-part content of a message=
.</p>

<p>This class consists of two main properties: <code translate=3D"no" dir=
=3D"ltr">role</code> and <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">parts</code>. T=
he <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">role</code>
property denotes the individual producing the content, while the <code tran=
slate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">parts</code>
property contains multiple elements, each representing a segment of data wi=
thin
a message.</p>

<div class=3D"devsite-table-wrapper"><table class=3D"responsive">
  <tbody><tr>
    <th colspan=3D"2">Parameters</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><p><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">role</code></p></td>
    <td><p>Optional: <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">string</code></p><p=
>The identity of the entity that
      creates the message. The following values are supported:</p>
      <ul>
      <li><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">user</code>: This indicates th=
at the message is sent by a real person, typically a user-generated message=
.</li>
      <li><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">model</code>: This indicates t=
hat the message is generated by the model.</li>
      </ul>
    <p>The <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">model</code> value is used to=
 insert messages from the model into the conversation during multi-turn con=
versations.</p><p>For non-multi-turn conversations, this field can be left =
blank or unset.</p></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><p><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">parts</code></p></td>
    <td><p><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">Part</code></p><p>A list of o=
rdered parts that make up a single message. Different parts may have differ=
ent <a href=3D"https://www.iana.org/assignments/media-types/media-types.xml=
">IANA MIME types</a>.</p><p>For limits on the inputs, such as the maximum =
number of tokens or the number of images, see the model specifications on t=
he <a href=3D"https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/generative-ai/docs/learn/m=
odels">Google models</a> page.</p><p>To compute the number of tokens in you=
r request, see <a href=3D"https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/generative-ai/=
docs/multimodal/get-token-count">Get token count</a>.</p></td>
  </tr>
</tbody></table></div>

<h4 id=3D"parts" data-text=3D"parts" tabindex=3D"-1" role=3D"presentation">=
<span class=3D"devsite-heading" role=3D"heading" aria-level=3D"4"><code tra=
nslate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">parts</code></span><button type=3D"button" class=
=3D"devsite-heading-link button-flat material-icons" aria-label=3D"Copy lin=
k to this section: parts" data-title=3D"Copy link to this section: parts" d=
ata-id=3D"parts"></button></h4>

<p>A data type containing media that is part of a multi-part <code translat=
e=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">Content</code> message.</p>

<div class=3D"devsite-table-wrapper"><table class=3D"responsive">
  <tbody><tr>
    <th colspan=3D"2">Parameters</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><p><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">text</code></p></td>
    <td><p>Optional: <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">string</code></p><p=
>A text prompt or code snippet.</p></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><p><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">inlineData</code></p></td>
    <td><p>Optional: <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">Blob</code></p><p>I=
nline data in raw bytes.</p><p>For <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">gemin=
i-1.0-pro-vision</code>, you can specify at most 1 image
      by using <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">inlineData</code>.To spec=
ify up to 16 images, use <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">fileData</code>=
.</p></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><p><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">fileData</code></p></td>
    <td><p>Optional: <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">fileData</code></p>=
<p>Data stored in a file.</p></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><p><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">functionCall</code></p></td>
    <td><p>Optional: <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">FunctionCall</code>=
.</p><p>It contains a string representing the <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D=
"ltr">FunctionDeclaration.name</code> field and a structured JSON object co=
ntaining any parameters for the function call predicted by the model.</p><p=
>See <a href=3D"https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/generative-ai/docs/model=
-reference/function-calling">Function calling</a>.</p></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><p><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">functionResponse</code></p></=
td>
    <td><p>Optional: <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">FunctionResponse</c=
ode>.</p><p>The result output of a <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">Funct=
ionCall</code> that contains a string representing the <code translate=3D"n=
o" dir=3D"ltr">FunctionDeclaration.name</code> field and a structured JSON =
object containing any output from the function call. It is used as context =
to the model.</p><p>See <a href=3D"https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/gener=
ative-ai/docs/model-reference/function-calling">Function calling</a>.</p></=
td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><p><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">videoMetadata</code></p></td>
    <td><p>Optional: <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">VideoMetadata</code=
></p><p>For video input, the start and end offset of the video in <a href=
=3D"https://protobuf.dev/reference/protobuf/google.protobuf/#duration">Dura=
tion</a> format. For example, to specify a 10 second clip starting at 1:00,=
 set <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">"startOffset": { "seconds": 60 }</c=
ode> and <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">"endOffset": { "seconds": 70 }<=
/code>.</p><p>The metadata should only be specified while the video data is=
 presented in <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">inlineData</code> or <code=
 translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">fileData</code>.</p></td>
  </tr>
</tbody></table></div>

<h4 id=3D"blob" data-text=3D"blob" tabindex=3D"-1" role=3D"presentation"><s=
pan class=3D"devsite-heading" role=3D"heading" aria-level=3D"4"><code trans=
late=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">blob</code></span><button type=3D"button" class=3D"=
devsite-heading-link button-flat material-icons" aria-label=3D"Copy link to=
 this section: blob" data-title=3D"Copy link to this section: blob" data-id=
=3D"blob"></button></h4>

<p>Content blob. If possible send as text rather than raw bytes.</p>

<div class=3D"devsite-table-wrapper"><table class=3D"responsive">
  <tbody><tr>
    <th colspan=3D"2">Parameters</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><p><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">mimeType</code></p></td>
    <td><p><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">string</code></p>
The media type of the file specified in the <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"l=
tr">data</code> or <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">fileUri</code>
fields. Acceptable values include the following:
<devsite-expandable id=3D"expandable-1"><a class=3D"exw-control" aria-contr=
ols=3D"expandable-1" aria-expanded=3D"false" tabindex=3D"0" role=3D"button"=
><p class=3D"showalways"><b>Click to expand MIME types</b></p></a>
 =20
  <ul>
    <li><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">application/pdf</code></li>
    <li><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">audio/mpeg</code></li>
    <li><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">audio/mp3</code></li>
    <li><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">audio/wav</code></li>
    <li><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">image/png</code></li>
    <li><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">image/jpeg</code></li>
    <li><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">image/webp</code></li>
    <li><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">text/plain</code></li>
    <li><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">video/mov</code></li>
    <li><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">video/mpeg</code></li>
    <li><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">video/mp4</code></li>
    <li><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">video/mpg</code></li>
    <li><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">video/avi</code></li>
    <li><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">video/wmv</code></li>
    <li><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">video/mpegps</code></li>
    <li><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">video/flv</code></li>
  </ul>
</devsite-expandable>
<p>For <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">gemini-1.0-pro-vision</code>, the=
 maximum video length is 2 minutes.</p><p>For Gemini&nbsp;1.5&nbsp;Pro and =
Gemini&nbsp;1.5&nbsp;Flash, the maximum length of an audio file is 8.4 hour=
s and the maximum length of a video file (without audio) is one hour. For m=
ore information, see <a href=3D"https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/generati=
ve-ai/docs/multimodal/send-multimodal-prompts#media_requirements">Gemini&nb=
sp;1.5&nbsp;Pro media requirements</a>.</p><p>Text files must be UTF-8 enco=
ded. The contents of the text file count toward the token limit.</p><p>Ther=
e is no limit on image resolution.</p></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><p><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">data</code></p></td>
    <td><p><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">bytes</code></p><p>
The <a href=3D"https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/generative-ai/docs/image/=
base64-encode">base64 encoding</a> of the image, PDF, or video
to include inline in the prompt. When including media inline, you must also=
 specify the media
type (<code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">mimeType</code>) of the data.
</p><p>Size limit: 20MB</p></td>
  </tr>
</tbody></table></div>

<h4 id=3D"filedata" data-text=3D"FileData" tabindex=3D"-1" role=3D"presenta=
tion"><span class=3D"devsite-heading" role=3D"heading" aria-level=3D"4">Fil=
eData</span><button type=3D"button" class=3D"devsite-heading-link button-fl=
at material-icons" aria-label=3D"Copy link to this section: FileData" data-=
title=3D"Copy link to this section: FileData" data-id=3D"filedata"></button=
></h4>

<p>URI or web-URL data.</p>

<div class=3D"devsite-table-wrapper"><table class=3D"responsive">
  <tbody><tr>
    <th colspan=3D"2">Parameters</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><p><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">mimeType</code></p></td>
    <td><p><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">string</code></p><p><a href=
=3D"https://www.iana.org/assignments/media-types/media-types.xml">IANA MIME=
 type</a> of the data.</p></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><p><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">fileUri</code></p></td>
    <td><p><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">string</code></p><p>
The URI or URL of the file to include in the prompt. Acceptable values incl=
ude the following:

</p><ul>
  <li><b>Cloud Storage bucket URI:</b> The object must either be publicly r=
eadable or reside in
    the same Google Cloud project that's sending the request. For <code tra=
nslate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">gemini-1.5-pro</code>
    and <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">gemini-1.5-flash</code>, the siz=
e limit is 2&nbsp;GB. For
    <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">gemini-1.0-pro-vision</code>, the si=
ze limit is 20&nbsp;MB.</li>
  <li><b>HTTP URL:</b> The file URL must be publicly readable. You can spec=
ify one video file, one
    audio file, and up to 10 image files per request. Audio files, video fi=
les, and documents can't
    exceed 15&nbsp;MB.</li>
  <li><b>YouTube video URL:</b>The YouTube video must be either owned by th=
e account that you used
    to sign in to the Google Cloud console or is public. Only one YouTube v=
ideo URL is supported per
    request.</li>
</ul>

<p>When specifying a <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">fileURI</code>, you=
 must also specify the media type
  (<code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">mimeType</code>) of the file. If VPC =
Service Controls is enabled, specifying a media file
  URL for <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">fileURI</code> is not supporte=
d.</p>
<p></p></td>
  </tr>
</tbody></table></div>

<h4 id=3D"functioncall" data-text=3D"functionCall" tabindex=3D"-1" role=3D"=
presentation"><span class=3D"devsite-heading" role=3D"heading" aria-level=
=3D"4"><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">functionCall</code></span><button=
 type=3D"button" class=3D"devsite-heading-link button-flat material-icons" =
aria-label=3D"Copy link to this section: functionCall" data-title=3D"Copy l=
ink to this section: functionCall" data-id=3D"functioncall"></button></h4>

<p>A predicted <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">functionCall</code> retur=
ned from the model that contains a string
representing the <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">functionDeclaration.nam=
e</code> and a structured JSON object
containing the parameters and their values.</p>

<div class=3D"devsite-table-wrapper"><table class=3D"responsive">
  <tbody><tr>
    <th colspan=3D"2">Parameters</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><p><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">name</code></p></td>
    <td><p><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">string</code></p><p>The name =
of the function to call.</p></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><p><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">args</code></p></td>
    <td><p><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">Struct</code></p><p>The funct=
ion parameters and values in JSON object format.</p><p>See <a href=3D"https=
://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/generative-ai/docs/model-reference/function-c=
alling">Function calling</a> for parameter details.</p></td>
  </tr>
</tbody></table></div>

<h4 id=3D"functionresponse" data-text=3D"functionResponse" tabindex=3D"-1" =
role=3D"presentation"><span class=3D"devsite-heading" role=3D"heading" aria=
-level=3D"4"><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">functionResponse</code></sp=
an><button type=3D"button" class=3D"devsite-heading-link button-flat materi=
al-icons" aria-label=3D"Copy link to this section: functionResponse" data-t=
itle=3D"Copy link to this section: functionResponse" data-id=3D"functionres=
ponse"></button></h4>

<p>The resulting output from a <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">FunctionC=
all</code> that contains a string representing the
<code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">FunctionDeclaration.name</code>. Also co=
ntains a structured JSON object with the
output from the function (and uses it as context for the model). This shoul=
d contain the
result of a <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">FunctionCall</code> made bas=
ed on model prediction.</p>

<div class=3D"devsite-table-wrapper"><table class=3D"responsive">
  <tbody><tr>
    <th colspan=3D"2">Parameters</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><p><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">name</code></p></td>
    <td><p><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">string</code></p><p>The name =
of the function to call.</p></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><p><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">response</code></p></td>
    <td><p><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">Struct</code></p><p>The funct=
ion response in JSON object format.</p></td>
  </tr>
</tbody></table></div>

<h4 id=3D"videometadata" data-text=3D"videoMetadata" tabindex=3D"-1" role=
=3D"presentation"><span class=3D"devsite-heading" role=3D"heading" aria-lev=
el=3D"4"><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">videoMetadata</code></span><but=
ton type=3D"button" class=3D"devsite-heading-link button-flat material-icon=
s" aria-label=3D"Copy link to this section: videoMetadata" data-title=3D"Co=
py link to this section: videoMetadata" data-id=3D"videometadata"></button>=
</h4>

<p>Metadata describing the input video content.</p>

<div class=3D"devsite-table-wrapper"><table class=3D"responsive">
  <tbody><tr>
    <th colspan=3D"2">Parameters</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><p><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">startOffset</code></p></td>
    <td><p>Optional: <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">google.protobuf.Dur=
ation</code></p><p>The start offset of the video.</p></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><p><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">endOffset</code></p></td>
    <td><p>Optional: <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">google.protobuf.Dur=
ation</code></p><p>The end offset of the video.</p></td>
  </tr>
</tbody></table></div>

<h4 id=3D"safetysetting" data-text=3D"safetySetting" tabindex=3D"-1" role=
=3D"presentation"><span class=3D"devsite-heading" role=3D"heading" aria-lev=
el=3D"4"><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">safetySetting</code></span><but=
ton type=3D"button" class=3D"devsite-heading-link button-flat material-icon=
s" aria-label=3D"Copy link to this section: safetySetting" data-title=3D"Co=
py link to this section: safetySetting" data-id=3D"safetysetting"></button>=
</h4>

<p>Safety settings.</p>

<div class=3D"devsite-table-wrapper"><table class=3D"responsive">
  <tbody><tr>
    <th colspan=3D"2">Parameters</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><p><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">category</code></p></td>
    <td><p>Optional: <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">HarmCategory</code>=
</p><p>
The safety category to configure a threshold for. Acceptable values include=
 the following:
<devsite-expandable id=3D"expandable-2"><a class=3D"exw-control" aria-contr=
ols=3D"expandable-2" aria-expanded=3D"false" tabindex=3D"0" role=3D"button"=
></a>
  </devsite-expandable></p><p class=3D"showalways"><b>Click to expand safet=
y categories</b></p>
  <ul>
    <li><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">HARM_CATEGORY_SEXUALLY_EXPLICIT<=
/code></li>
    <li><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">HARM_CATEGORY_HATE_SPEECH</code>=
</li>
    <li><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">HARM_CATEGORY_HARASSMENT</code><=
/li>
    <li><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">HARM_CATEGORY_DANGEROUS_CONTENT<=
/code></li>
  </ul>

<p></p></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><p><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">threshold</code></p></td>
    <td><p>Optional: <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">HarmBlockThreshold<=
/code></p><p>The threshold for blocking responses that could belong to the =
specified safety category based on probability.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">OFF</code></li>
        <li><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">BLOCK_NONE</code></li>
        <li><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">BLOCK_LOW_AND_ABOVE</code></=
li>
        <li><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">BLOCK_MEDIUM_AND_ABOVE</code=
></li>
        <li><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">BLOCK_ONLY_HIGH</code></li>
      </ul></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><p><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">method</code></p></td>
    <td><p>Optional: <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">HarmBlockMethod</co=
de></p><p>Specify if the threshold is used for probability or severity scor=
e. If not specified, the threshold is used for probability score.</p></td>
  </tr>
</tbody></table></div>

<h4 id=3D"harmcategory" data-text=3D"harmCategory" tabindex=3D"-1" role=3D"=
presentation"><span class=3D"devsite-heading" role=3D"heading" aria-level=
=3D"4"><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">harmCategory</code></span><button=
 type=3D"button" class=3D"devsite-heading-link button-flat material-icons" =
aria-label=3D"Copy link to this section: harmCategory" data-title=3D"Copy l=
ink to this section: harmCategory" data-id=3D"harmcategory"></button></h4>

<p>Harm categories that block content.</p>

<div class=3D"devsite-table-wrapper"><table class=3D"responsive">
  <tbody><tr>
    <th colspan=3D"2">Parameters</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><p><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">HARM_CATEGORY_UNSPECIFIED</co=
de></p></td>
    <td><p>The harm category is unspecified.</p></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><p><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">HARM_CATEGORY_HATE_SPEECH</co=
de></p></td>
    <td><p>The harm category is hate speech.</p></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><p><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">HARM_CATEGORY_DANGEROUS_CONTE=
NT</code></p></td>
    <td><p>The harm category is dangerous content.</p></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><p><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">HARM_CATEGORY_HARASSMENT</cod=
e></p></td>
    <td><p>The harm category is harassment.</p></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><p><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">HARM_CATEGORY_SEXUALLY_EXPLIC=
IT</code></p></td>
